nodecode-flipletters is a rewrite of Terahertz-Inc's Terahertz-Inc/flipletters-mcp:

  https://github.com/Terahertz-Inc/flipletters-mcp
  commit 460880225ce2f7b95b1020622b2552aaa1a580b2
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Terahertz, Inc. (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the whole repository at that commit: a manifest, an
MCP server entry, a skill and a README, with no executable code of its own.
What it described is a hosted Model Context Protocol server at
https://app.flipletters.com/mcp/v1, and the cell speaks to that same server
over the same wire. Carried over: the endpoint and the Bearer flk_ key the
manifest's mcp.json names; MCP over Streamable HTTP (one POST per JSON-RPC
message, an event stream's last data payload as the answer, the
Mcp-Session-Id echoed, a dropped session made again); tools/list and
tools/call; the thirteen tools the server serves -- flipletters_flipcode_
reference, example_board, validate_board, template_url, create_animation,
render_board, render_status, list_teams, share_to_team, list_workspaces,
list_postiz_destinations, list_postiz_integrations and share_to_postiz --
with the argument names their input schemas give, camelCase included; and
the skill's own order of work (read the reference, draft, validate, render
or share only when asked). LICENSE is the repository's LICENSE, unchanged.

What was left out, and why: the Hermes and Cursor manifest extensions
(plugin.json's server trust flag, the .cursor-plugin variables) and the
skills/flipletters front matter, because Nodecode has no plugin manifest and
one skill folder, so the same guidance is the cell's (help :flipletters)
primer and the /flipletters command instead; the local stdio variant
(npx flipletters-mcp-server), because the cell speaks to the hosted server
directly and installs nothing; PUBLISHING.md and server.json, which are the
listing repository's own release paperwork rather than a user-facing
feature. One tool was added: flipletters_tools, which lists what the live
server offers this key, because the tool set is served at run time and the
cell should not be the place its schema goes stale.
